<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal and Parliamentary Titles Act 1927</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1927">1927</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal and Parliamentary Titles Act 1927 was an act of the UK Parliament that changed the formal name of the state to the United <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain</a> and Northern Ireland, recognising the separation of the Irish Free State in 1922. It also allowed the royal style and titles to be altered accordingly by proclamation.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Royal and Parliamentary Titles Act</b> of 1927 changed the formal name to the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-kingdom">United Kingdom · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The remaining state was formally renamed the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland by the <b>Royal and Parliamentary Titles Act</b> of 1927.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
